====By-elections====
Three seats were left vacant, with no election taking place in constituencies 5, 12 and 92 (Western Area Rural District). The election was delayed in Western Area Rural District due to the death of [[People's Movement for Democratic Change|PMDC]] candidate, and a by-election was held on 9 February 2013. The result was a victory for the [[All People's Congress|APC]] candidate, who received 61% of the vote.<ref>[http://www.nec-sierraleone.org/index_files/Parliamentary_Results/PRESS%20RELEASE_Const%2092.pdf Declaration of Parliamentary Election Results in Constituency 92] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304055830/http://www.nec-sierraleone.org/index_files/Parliamentary_Results/PRESS%20RELEASE_Const%2092.pdf |date=2016-03-04 }} National Electoral Commission</ref>

==Aftermath==
Results showed Koroma winning in the first round of voting, receiving 58.7% of the vote against 37.4% for the SLPP candidate, Bio. If he had received less than 55% of the vote, a second round would have been necessary. Following the announcement of results, Koroma was promptly sworn in for another term as President on 23 November 2012. He said that he would "continue to attract investment" and "continue to fight corruption".<ref>{{Deprecated archive|url=https://archive.today/20130416013719/http://www.trust.org/alertnet/news/sierra-leones-koroma-promises-growth-in-new-term/|title=Sierra Leone's Koroma promises growth in new term}} Reuters, 23 November 2012</ref>

